text:
nora-cs: Ignite onboarding hit a wall. Android app rollout -> many 401 then rapid 429s during SDK.init. ~220 devices after update.

devin-platform: Can you paste a short log snippet and SDK version? Ephemeral tokens or long-lived?

nora-cs: android-sdk 1.4.0, ephemeral tokens via /session. Snippet:

```
I/Client: POST /v1/chat 401 auth_missing
I/Client: fetching session token
I/Client: POST /v1/chat 429 rate_limit window=60s
```

They call SDK.init() from multiple activities without awaiting token promise.

ari-eng: Sounds like preflight stampede + retry amplification. Quick checks: (1) do they await token before issuing requests? (2) is Authorization injected per-request via interceptor? (3) aggressive immediate retries on 401?

kevin-support: Customer-facing quick fixes we recommend: serialize init (single entry), add small randomized jitter (200-2000ms) after token fetch before heavy calls, reduce preflight concurrency (3-4), enable preflight coalescing, and change retry policy to refresh-once + exponential backoff.

devin-platform: Server-side short-term workaround: have their token endpoint return the same recent ephemeral token for a brief window (2-5s) during bursts or gate issuance with a tiny semaphore. Long-term: update mobile onboarding docs with code patterns.

ari-eng: Minimal code pattern we share:

```
// guard single init
if (initLock.compareAndSet(false, true)) {
  executor.execute(() -> {
    String t = fetchTokenBlocking();
    Thread.sleep(random(200,1200)); // jitter
    sdk.initWithToken(t);
    initLock.set(false);
  });
}
// interceptor adds Authorization header per request
```

kevin-support: I'll DM KB and suggested SDK flags. Nora, cc me on the reply so I can include a one-pager about rate windows and mobile flags.

metrics-bot: [alert] edge.rate.ignite spike -> 429s +340% in 5m.

nora-cs: Customer applied single-init + 1s jitter + set maxPreflight=3. They reported 429s dropped to baseline. Closing loop; will add note to onboarding checklist. Thanks team :thumbsup:
